    {
      "id": "be-s7-budget-constraint-c1",
      "heading": "Opportunity set and budget line",
      "explanation_md": "The **budget constraint** has two parts:\n\n- **Opportunity set**: the set of consumption bundles that are **affordable**: **PxX + PyY ≤ M**.\n- **Budget line**: the bundles that **exhaust the consumer's income**: **PxX + PyY = M**.\n\nOn the graph (good Y on the vertical axis, good X on the horizontal axis) the budget line is a straight line and the opportunity set is the area under it.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [
        {
          "term": "Opportunity set",
          "meaning": "The set of consumption bundles that are affordable: PxX + PyY ≤ M.",
          "source_ref": "be--session-7#10"
        },
        {
          "term": "Budget line",
          "meaning": "The bundles of goods that exhaust a consumer's income: PxX + PyY = M.",
          "source_ref": "be--session-7#10"
        }
      ],
      "exam_line": "Opportunity set: PxX + PyY ≤ M. Budget line: PxX + PyY = M.",
