    {
      "id": "be-s7-budget-constraint-c2",
      "heading": "Intercepts and slope: the market rate of substitution",
      "explanation_md": "Solve the budget line for Y:\n\n**Y = M/Py - (Px/Py) X**\n\n- **Vertical intercept**: **M/Py** (spend all income on Y).\n- **Horizontal intercept**: **M/Px** (spend all income on X).\n- **Slope**: **Px/Py** in size. The slope of the budget line is the **market rate of substitution**.\n\nThe consumer's own willingness to swap is the marginal rate of substitution (indifference curve); the **market rate** is Px/Py (budget line).",
