    {
      "id": "be-s7-budget-constraint-c3",
      "heading": "Shifts in the budget line",
      "explanation_md": "**Income changes:**\n\n- An **increase** in income gives a **parallel, outward shift** of the budget line (M1 > M0).\n- A **decrease** gives a **parallel, downward shift** (M2 < M0).\n\n**Price changes:**\n\n- A **decrease** in the price of X **rotates the budget line counter-clockwise** (Px0 > Px1). The Y intercept M0/Py stays put, and the X intercept moves out from M0/Px0 to M0/Px1.\n- An **increase** rotates it **clockwise**.\n\nSo: income change = **parallel shift**; price change = **rotation**.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Income up: parallel outward shift; income down: parallel downward shift. Price of X down: counter-clockwise rotation; price up: clockwise.",
      "clarification": null,
